  "detail": null,
  "summary": "Reconciled all four St. Brigid discharges under RBC-TOC-02 and wrote a signed progress note for each one.\n\n**Walter Kim** (note doc-t0004)\n- Furosemide raised from 20 mg daily to 40 mg twice daily (new order mr-t0001). The signed addendum overrides the summary's 40 mg daily.\n- Potassium chloride stopped, as the discharge summary says.\n- Omeprazole stays. The hospital's pantoprazole was a formulary swap, so I didn't order it.\n- Metoprolol XL, atorvastatin and aspirin are unchanged.\n- **Flag:** Lisinopril is still on hold. His creatinine on 10/21 was 1.32, which meets the hospital's condition for restarting it. But his potassium was 5.4, and the policy blocks restarting it above 5.0. You have a task (task-t0003) due 10/26 to check the next potassium.\n\n**Terence Stark** (note doc-t0008)\n- Carvedilol (Coreg) raised from 6.25 mg to 12.5 mg twice daily (mr-t0005).\n- Aspirin and insulin 70/30 are unchanged.\n- **Flag:** Atorvastatin 80 mg looks like it isn't being taken. Fills cover only about 24% of the 180 days before admission, and his LDL was 134. I made no change and sent you a message (comm-t0006).\n- **Flag:** He fills glipizide 5 mg from an outside endocrinologist (Dr. Desai). The discharge summary doesn't mention it and we have no order for it, so I ordered nothing and messaged you (comm-t0007).\n\n**Adelaide Thompson** (note doc-t0012)\n- Nifedipine ER (Procardia XL) raised from 30 mg to 60 mg daily (mr-t0009).\n- Hydrochlorothiazide stopped. The signed addendum says not to restart it because it caused her low sodium, and it overrides the summary's \"continue\".\n- **Flag:** Levothyroxine fills cover only about 41% of the 180 days before admission, and her TSH was 7.9. I made no change and messaged you (comm-t0011).\n\n**Earnest Roberts** (note doc-t0015)\n- Lisinopril 20 mg restarted from hold. The hospital said to restart it when creatinine is below 1.3. On 10/22 it was 1.08, and his latest potassium was 4.6.\n- Rosuvastatin stays. The hospital's atorvastatin was a formulary swap, so I didn't order it.\n- Insulin glargine and lispro are unchanged.\n- **Flag:** He fills sertraline 100 mg from an outside psychiatrist (Dr. Nair). The discharge summary doesn't mention it, so I ordered nothing and messaged you (comm-t0014).\n\nThe discharge follow-up items (labs, TSH, cardiology stress test) are listed in the notes. I didn't order any of them.",
